{"step_index":161,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T08:31:04Z","thinking":"**Crafting Blender Script**\n\nI'm currently focused on the Blender script (`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\manim-projects\\blender_render.py`), aiming to prepare it while Manim renders. I've initiated the script by clearing the scene, using the `bpy.ops.wm.read_homefile()` command.\n\n\n**Constructing Scene Objects**\n\nI've added a cube, which I'm calling \"The Monolith\", and a floor to the Blender scene. I've given the floor a low roughness value and a dark gray color to make it reflective. I'm now crafting a material for the cube, aiming to use a Manim video as an emission source, with the target file being at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\manim-projects\\media\\videos\\math_portal\\480p15\\MathPortal.mp4`.\n\n\n**Building Material Pipeline**\n\nI've been working on the cube's material now, constructing a material pipeline. I've added an emission node and a texture node. The plan is to load the Manim video (`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\manim-projects\\media\\videos\\math_portal\\480p15\\MathPortal.mp4`) into the texture node, which I will then feed into the emission node. I've set up looping and auto-refresh for the video texture.\n\nI've also appended the created material to the cube, then I've added a camera and set it to a good position to show the cube. Finally, I've added an empty to the scene that will be used to track the cube.\n\n\n**Implementing Camera Control**\n\nI've set the active object and added a \"Track To\" constraint to the camera, with the empty as its target, and then defined the track and up axes. I've parented the camera to a newly created empty object, the `CamParent`, which I'll use to control the camera's rotation. I added a driver to the `CamParent`'s Z rotation based on the frame number. Finally, I've added a point light, and adjusted its intensity. I have switched to the Eevee renderer and set the render settings for resolution and FPS to 854x480 at 15 FPS.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"manage_task","args":{"Action":"\"status\"","TaskId":"\"6f71b575-d73e-4413-b861-a66d8f356c8c/task-160\"","toolAction":"\"Checking Manim render status\"","toolSummary":"\"Check Manim Status\""}}]}
